--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ friend B \(no keyword\) may write A's private: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
is not accessible
--
N5008 [class.friend]/3: a friend declaration naming a class via a
simple-type-specifier (`friend B;`, no class/struct keyword) befriends that
class.  Previously CBMC's parser dropped this form, denying the friend access to
private members.
